A||N||4||Dick Martin||Isuzu-5 speed to a Quad-4||||5||
Z||000000||Dick Martin||08-18-2001||03:04 PM||||Got a Quad-4 going in a Fiero to run at Bonneville and want the highest final drive. Been told that an Isuzu transaxle will work. Can I bolt it in as easy as the GM transaxle Getrag type? Anyone done one? If so what year Isuzu will work.||||reg||5
Z||000001||pherder||08-18-2001||04:22 PM||||An Isuzu from a Sunfire/Cavalier with the TwinCam engine will bolt to the Quad 4.  Not sure if the 2.2 engine has the Quad 4 bolt pattern.<P>That transaxle has the 3.35:1 FDR which is the best available for what you are trying to do.  That is what I had in my 88 Coupe that Standard owns now.<P>The stock EPROM has a speed limiter that is set at ~ 112 mph ... ask Standard ... he found it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"><P>BTW, I have a MantaPart SCX W41 EPROM with the mph limiter turn off (actually it is set for a REAL high reading!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) that will work with a 93 Quad 4 ECM and a 93 ECM for sale.  $150 for both, $100 for the chip and $50 for the ECM (no chip).<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||08-18-2001||08:27 PM||||Yeah, that speed limiter was kind of a surprise..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>As for the tranny, at 90mph in 5th gear I'm at 3,000rpm.  Just barely in the powerband.  3rd gear pulls hard up to a little over 100, and 4th was still pulling when I hit the limiter.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodney||08-19-2001||07:58 AM||||The final actual drive ratio is the 5th gear ratio X the ring and pinion drive ratio. On the Getrag it is .72 X 3.61 which is 2.60. Anyone know the 5th gear ratio on this new Isuzu??  3.35 X __ = ???||||reg||1
Z||000004||pherder||08-19-2001||09:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rodney:<BR><B>The final actual drive ratio is the 5th gear ratio X the ring and pinion drive ratio. On the Getrag it is .72 X 3.61 which is 2.60. Anyone know the 5th gear ratio on this new Isuzu??  3.35 X __ = ???</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It is exactly the same as the Fiero's Isuzu 5 speed (same gearing)<P><BR>Isuzu MT2 - 3.35 final drive gears 1-5<BR>     3.73   2.04   1.45   1.03   0.74<P>Or to answer Rodney's question ... <P>3.35 x 0.74 = 2.479<P>Paul||||reg||1
